# Project vision

AI Agent Control Platform — Vision Document
Overview
We’re building a unified control platform for managing AI agents as stateless, deployable applications. The platform enables users to create, launch, stop, and interact with agents — while managing communication flow, container lifecycle, and conversation history.

Agents are deployed in Docker containers and operate independently, while the platform acts as the control plane for routing messages, storing conversation data, and optionally managing state.

Core Concepts
Agents as Stateless Apps
Agents are treated as independent, stateless containers.

The platform proxies all chats to the appropriate agent and logs interactions.

Agents can optionally retrieve state from the platform using a conversation ID.

Key Features (MVP)
1. Agent Lifecycle Management
List all agents in a dashboard

Launch and stop agents via Docker containers

Health check via a simple /healthz endpoint exposed by the agent

2. Agent Creation
Two modes when creating an agent:

Externally hosted: User provides the endpoint of an already-running agent

Internally deployed: User supplies metadata, and the platform generates a Dockerfile, builds the image, and handles deployment

Metadata fields for Dockerfile generation (e.g. base image, command, dependencies) will be defined separately

3. Chat Routing & Communication
All user messages are routed through the platform to the correct agent

The platform acts as a proxy, managing communication and request formatting

Agents remain stateless, but can fetch conversation history via:
GET /state?conversation_id=xyz

4. Conversation Management
The platform logs all messages between users and agents in a database

Agents can optionally use this data to load or manage their own memory/state

5. Chat Interface (Initial Version)
A simple, clean interface per agent for user interaction

Each message includes:

Thought process (optional)

Tool use (optional)

Final answer (required)

UI will evolve based on agent behavior and memory integration in the future

Technical Architecture Summary
Platform Runtime: Docker + Docker Compose

Agent Deployment: Containers launched/stopped by the platform via Docker

Templates: Agents defined using user-supplied metadata → converted into Dockerfiles

Chat Routing: Platform proxies all user-agent communications

Health Checks: Agents expose a basic /healthz endpoint

State Retrieval: Agents use a REST endpoint to optionally load past messages

Database: Stores all chat interactions per conversation

Deferred / Future Features
These are out of scope for the initial release but earmarked for future development:

User authentication and role-based permissions

Memory management (summaries, embeddings, RAG)

Agent templates with UI abstraction

Multi-agent coordination

Analytics and usage reporting

File/object storage for agent reference

Vision Summary
A lightweight but powerful control platform for deploying, managing, and interacting with stateless AI agents. It handles routing, logging, and lifecycle management — making it easy to build, chat with, and scale intelligent agents from a single interface.

